# legacy-peer-deps is intentionally NOT set.
#
# It used to be `legacy-peer-deps=true` to mask a few dependencies whose declared
# peer ranges lag the repo's versions (React 19, TypeScript 6). Those are now
# resolved explicitly via "overrides" in package.json ($react / $typescript), so
# npm can install with full (strict) peer resolution again.
#
# Do NOT re-add legacy-peer-deps: it disables npm `overrides` entirely, which would
# silently drop both the peer-range fixes AND the esbuild/ws/form-data security pins.
